WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.720
One kind of cell tells you a violin is playing, and that your head just turned

2
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.720
toward it.

3
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:15.390
On top of each hair cell sits a bundle of stiff stereocilia, graded in height like a

4
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.390
staircase.

5
00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:19.833
Fine tip links join each shorter one to its taller neighbour.

6
00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:25.163
At rest, the links carry some tension, so some channels are already open.

7
00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:27.983
Here, take a cell with only a few open.

8
00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:31.447
Push the bundle toward its tallest stereocilia.

9
00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:35.707
The links tighten, more channels open, and the cell depolarizes.

10
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:38.337
Now push it the other way.

11
00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:40.157
What happens to the current?

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.300
The few channels open at rest close.

13
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.820
Less current flows in, and the cell hyperpolarizes.

14
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.580
But the effect is lopsided.

15
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.440
There is less room to reduce the current than to increase it, because only the

16
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.300
channels open at rest can close.

17
00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:03.673
What carries the current?

18
00:01:04.513 --> 00:01:06.753
The hair cell's two ends sit in two different fluids.

19
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.473
The top faces endolymph.

20
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:14.993
It is rich in K⁺, and in the cochlea it is held about +80 mV positive.

21
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.187
The base faces perilymph, which is low in K⁺.

22
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:24.310
Across the top, the inside is far more negative than the endolymph.

23
00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.630
So K⁺ is pushed in, hard.

24
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.110
Across the base, K⁺ leaves through potassium channels.

25
00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.410
In this steady picture, as much leaves as enters.

26
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:37.963
So K⁺ runs downhill the whole way.

27
00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.403
The battery is in the wall of the cochlea, not in the cell.

28
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:45.057
The cell's voltage settles where two pulls balance.

29
00:01:46.077 --> 00:01:47.937
Open transduction channels pull it up.

30
00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.150
Basal potassium channels pull it down.

31
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.450
Moving the bundle changes the top pull directly.

32
00:01:56.383 --> 00:02:01.883
Depolarization opens calcium channels at the base, and calcium entry drives

33
00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:03.963
transmitter release onto the nerve fibre.

34
00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:09.907
So a hair cell's first response reports which way, and how far, its bundle is

35
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:10.907
pushed.

36
00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:15.447
What that means depends on what pushes the bundle, and on the circuits that read the

37
00:02:15.447 --> 00:02:15.667
cell.
